Mythix curated TkG layer for the mythix-11.19 profile
=====================================================

Source  : Kron4ek/wine-tkg tag 11.19 (b471df7dc4f2), minus vanilla wine-11.19 + wine-staging v11.19 (766285c4)
Target  : Valve wine 1c78596625336a73dbfc035dbbcf0dbdd95b06eb + GE a3f58c5 protonprep (staging v11.0)
Applies : cleanly on top of the GE layer (git apply), no fuzz

Kept (TkG-only behaviour not already in Valve/GE):
  * programs/explorer/desktop.c   — Wayland-first default driver ("mac,wayland,x11")
  * loader/wine.inf.in            — [CustomOverrides]: ddraw/winhttp/winmm/version native-first
  * dlls/ntdll/unix/debug.c       — WINEDEBUG defaults to -all when unset
  * dlls/user32/Makefile.in       — user32 at the Windows image base on i386
  * dlls/kernelbase/loader.c      — MUI resource lookup for localized resources
  * dlls/win32k.sys/win32k.sys.spec — real forwards instead of stubs on 64-bit
  * programs/winecfg/*            — TkG Staging tab (CSMT toggle semantics)
Mythix:
  * dlls/ntdll/loader.c           — Mythix testing-build banner instead of the stock staging one

Dropped on purpose (already in Valve/GE, or conflicts with them):
  * wine64 loader naming (configure.ac, loader/Makefile.in, ntdll/unix/loader.c) — Valve uses loader64/;
    applying TkG's on top is what caused the old "duplicate wine64 install" fix 26
  * LAA override + wine_nt_to_unix_file_name syscall exports (ntdll.spec, ntsyscalls.h, wow64, virtual.c)
    — Valve has its own WINE_LARGE_ADDRESS_AWARE path and wine_nt_to_unix_file_name
  * EAC/BattlEye bits (kernelbase, loadorder, sechost, belauncher, wineboot) — already in Valve
  * winebus DisableHidraw/DisableInput default-on — would disable hidraw (DualSense/DS4 haptics, Mythix DS4 work)
  * dcomp/dxgi composition reverts — Kron4ek staging exclusions, not TkG features
  * NTSync banner — Valve already prints "ntsync: up and running."
  * wine/heap.h compat header and its users; TkG's hardcoded version string (Mythix brands its own)

